# Unified Data Tab — Implementation Plan

Consolidate the current 5-tab navigation (`Dashboard`, `Company Media`, `Macro Sentiment`, `Deep Analysis`, `Portfolio`) into 3 tabs (`Data`, `Deep Analysis`, `Portfolio`). The new **Data** tab becomes the single hub for browsing and selectively fetching all company-level raw data, plus a dedicated YouTube channel insights sub-tab. All fetched data is persisted to local disk caches so Deep Analysis can reuse it without redundant API calls.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Tab deletion scope**: The existing `Dashboard` (FilingDashboard), `Company Media`, and `Macro Sentiment` views will be **replaced** by the new Data tab. Their functionality (financials viewer, news feed, earnings transcript viewer, YouTube video list, macro sentiment gauge) will be absorbed into the Data tab's sub-panels. The original view files will be deleted.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Header simplification**: The current Header has `🔎 Fetch from SEC` and `📁 Upload PDF` buttons that open `UploadModal`. These will be **removed from the header** and replaced by the Data tab's built-in fetch control panel. The `UploadModal` component remains for manual PDF upload but is accessed from within the Data tab, not the header.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **8-K / Form 4 data**: The `findata` package already has `get_insider_trades(ticker, count)` for Form 4 and `find_filings(ticker, form_type="8-K", ...)` for 8-K metadata. Full 8-K body text extraction is **not** supported by `findata` — the initial implementation will fetch 8-K metadata + filing links (title, date, URL) and Form 4 structured trade data. Full 8-K text parsing could be added later.

