#### [MODIFY] [`backend/services/pipeline.py`](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/pipeline.py)

Make each agent's data-fetching step **cache-first**: before calling the external API, check the corresponding disk cache. If cached data exists and covers the requested date range, use it directly.

**Changes per agent initialization in `analyze_pipeline()`:**

| Agent | Currently fetches from | Change |
|-------|----------------------|--------|
| `sec_filings` | In-memory `CompanyStore` | Already cache-first via `filing_cache.rehydrate_company_store()` — no change needed |
| `technical_analysis` | `price_provider.fetch_technical_data()` (live Yahoo Finance) | Check `price_cache` first; fall back to live fetch and cache result |
| `earnings_call` | `news_provider.search_earnings_transcript()` (live Tavily) | Already cache-first via `transcript_cache` — no change needed |
| `company_news` | `news_provider.search_company_news()` (live Tavily) | Check `news_cache` first; fall back to live fetch and cache result |
| `macro_market` | `news_provider.search_macro_news()` (live Tavily) | Lower priority — macro news is time-sensitive; optionally cache |
| `youtube_analysis` | `youtube_provider` (live YouTube API) | Lower priority — videos are time-sensitive |

The key change: wrap each agent's data-fetching call inside a helper that reads cache → falls back to live fetch → writes cache. This is done in the agent's `analyze()` method or in a shared `services/data_fetcher.py` orchestrator.

