#### [NEW] [`backend/routers/data.py`](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/routers/data.py)

New router that exposes **selective data fetching** — the frontend can request any combination of the 5 data types for a given ticker + date range in a single call.

```python
# POST /data/fetch
class DataFetchRequest(BaseModel):
    ticker: str
    start_date: str              # YYYY-MM-DD
    end_date: str                # YYYY-MM-DD
    include: list[str]           # subset of: ["sec_10k_10q", "sec_other", "news", "earnings", "price"]
    force_refresh: bool = False  # bypass cache

class DataFetchResponse(BaseModel):
    ticker: str
    results: dict[str, DataFetchResult]  # keyed by data type

class DataFetchResult(BaseModel):
    status: str       # "ok" | "cached" | "error" | "skipped"
    message: str | None = None
    count: int = 0    # number of items fetched/loaded
```

- `GET /data/status/{ticker}` — returns which data types are cached for this ticker and their date ranges. The frontend uses this to show filled/empty indicators on each data-type checkbox.
- `GET /data/news/{ticker}` — return cached news articles (read-only, no fetch)
- `GET /data/price/{ticker}` — return cached price/technical data (read-only)
- `GET /data/insider/{ticker}` — return cached Form 4 + 8-K data (read-only)

The existing `GET /media/earnings`, `GET /periods`, `GET /financials` endpoints remain unchanged — they already serve the SEC + earnings data that the Data tab's viewer panels will consume.

